{"title":"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_27\">Problem 27</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 27\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If an angle of a triangle remains unchanged but each of its two including sides is doubled, then the area is multiplied by: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b769a23daffd9da2778b9a1e8db6721547aaf9ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 3 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 6 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{more than }6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"429\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the angle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the sides around it be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. \nThe area of the triangle can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f4351ef2c0dee5f30be832935220e90867f1ba01.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A =\\frac{a \\cdot b \\cdot \\sin(\\theta)}{2}\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"38\" />\nThe doubled sides have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6ea4756efa52a156029529aba37a305a5cb496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b30259d95f64f9aa7c6bd36e1583618a23c8bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />, while the angle is still <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the area is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390685ef8590ce61cc3efaecc3584d241561f5eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2a \\cdot 2b \\cdot \\sin(\\theta)}{2}\\]\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/7/86703e392c386dfa6c7aa27865862857f191fc6b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rrightarrow  \\frac{4ab \\sin \\theta}{2} = 4A\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/1/9d1e11b199804f447fcd3a22d97c17ebbe9f963f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed {C}\\]\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>~JustinLee2017 \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME\" title=\"1956 AHSME\">1956 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1956 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1956\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Proble